<text fill="var(--svugy-text)" font-size="17" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start" textLength="174.242" x="-533.472" y="80.726">svugy · how it is built</text>
<text fill="var(--svugy-text-muted)" font-size="11.5" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start" textLength="266.319" x="-533.472" y="98.726">text in → model → layout → geometry → SVG out</text>
<text fill="var(--svugy-text)" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="start" textLength="103.973" x="1106.923" y="76.367">Read it as a story</text>
<text fill="var(--svugy-text-muted)" font-size="11" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start" textLength="159.897" x="1106.923" y="96.367">① your text becomes a model</text>
<text fill="var(--svugy-text-muted)" font-size="11" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start" textLength="227.595" x="1106.923" y="113.367">② the model becomes boxes in plan space</text>
<text fill="var(--svugy-text-muted)" font-size="11" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start" textLength="186.538" x="1106.923" y="130.367">③ boxes become isometric shapes</text>
<text fill="var(--svugy-text-muted)" font-size="11" font-weight="400" text-anchor="start" textLength="248.042" x="1106.923" y="147.367">④ shapes become one SVG file, runtime inside</text>
